How to define a function in Racket:
    (define (f x) (+ (* x x) (* 3 x) 4))
    (define (g x y)
        (+ (sqr x) (* 6 x y) (sqr y) (* 9 x) (- (* 3 y)) -100))

function definition:
    - name for the function
    - list of parameters
    - body expression

    Ex. (define (g x y)
            (+ x y))
        //(g 1 2) outputs: 3

predicates:
    the functions that produce Bool values are called predicates
    
    By convention, the names of predicates end in a ""

    Ex. (define (cold? t)
            (< t 8))

identifiers:
    three rules of identifiers:
        1. identifiers can contain letters, numbers, -, _, ., ?, =, and alphabetic
        2. identifiers cannot contain spaces, brackets and quotation marks
        3. must contain at least one non-number

syntax:
    is the form of a program: which sequences of symbols constitute valid programs

semantics: 
    is the meaning of a program: what happens when a syntactically valid program is evaluated




